### `Managed-route destination unreachable (502 after full timeout)`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Proxy 502s off-subnet ZT prefixes (e.g. LAN behind a gateway node) after a ~10s hang; same target works in VPN mode; `zts_connect` returns `-1` only after the full timeout | ZeroTierOne applies managed routes at OS level only — libzt's lwIP has no route (`ERR_RTE`), and `zts_connect` retries fresh connects for the whole timeout, hiding the instant failure | `LWIP_HOOK_IP4_ROUTE`/`IP6_ROUTE` (netif by longest prefix) + `LWIP_HOOK_ETHARP_GET_GW`/`ND6_GET_GW` (off-link dest → resolve the route's `via` on the overlay; via-less → dest itself) in `libzt/src/Routing.cpp`, fed by `NodeService::rebuildRouteCache()`; policy = `OneService::checkIfManagedIsAllowed` (port verbatim, keep in sync); rebuild AAR. Recognition: a **full-timeout `zts_connect` hang == no route/stack problem**, not a slow peer |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `BufferedReader eats the request body (plain-HTTP proxy)`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| POST/PUT through the proxy fails (origin 400/500, form login loops or redirects) while GETs, CONNECT, and VPN mode all work | Header parsing with `BufferedReader` then relaying the **raw** socket stream: body bytes read ahead into the reader's 8KB buffer are silently dropped | Parse headers byte-exact from a `BufferedInputStream` up to CRLF-CRLF and relay from the **same** stream object. Differential test: plain POST fails while an `Expect: 100-continue` POST (body sent after headers) works |

